 + Run 'make clean' at /path_to_clam_repository/packages folder  

 + For each clam package, check the following files
	1) changelog 
	2) changelog.Debian
	3) copyright
	4) control (do not worry now for dependencies)
	5) shlibs
	6) Makefile

 + Run 'make init' at /path_to_clam_repository/packages folder 
  
 + Compile clam binaries modules setting the prefix to
	/path_to_clam_repository/packages/Debian/lib<clam module name>0-dev/debian/usr

 + Install CLAM packages issuing a command like:
	$ scons prefix=/home/mramirez/Sandboxes/CLAM-nh/packages/Debian/libclamcore0-dev/debian/usr release=yes xmlbackend=xercesc install_core

 + Check that the list of package dependencies listed on the control file
   matches actual binaries dependencies
	+ Execute the command:
		$ objdump -p debian/usr/lib/*so* | grep NEEDED
    + For each shared object listed execute and write down the package names:
		$ dpkg -S <shared object name>
	+ Now, for each package name execute and write down the installed package version:
		$ apt-cache showpkg <package name> | head
 	+ Update control file accordingly to the dependency list obtained, having in mind
	  the following:
		+ When specifying package version requirements only consider version numbers up
		  to the minor version number

 + Run 'make dist' at at /path_to_clam_repository/packages folder
 
 + Fix issues reported by lintian 
